<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dickinsonia-costata-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Dickinsonia costata cellular Turing wavelength, 56 µm, White Sea 558 Ma (Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 85.9/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the Schnakenberg septal model (Du=0.05, Dv=0.55, a=0.12, b=0.88, seed 3167) and anchors the measured peak at 5.564e-5 m (55.64 µm). Across eight diffusivity scales, measured wavenumber versus linear fastest wavenumber has Pearson r = 0.999999999886, wavelength RMSE 0.061 µm against 55.64*sqrt(s), and KS = 0.125. Equal diffusion decays to roundoff (reported ratio 4215 after flooring the control std at 1e-4). The growth GIF is 12 frames at 720x540 and ends on the CC BY 2.5 fossil (CV similarity 96.0). A gradient-energy ellipse on that photograph has aspect 1.8 and Ramanujan circularity 0.882. k_meas/k_m remains 1.037: the nonlinear peak sits slightly off the linear fastest mode. Overall 85.9/100 (faithfulness 84.3, reproducibility 89.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/dickinsonia_costata_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-dickinsonia-costata-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 914350 B, 1440×984 px, artifact_sha256 35aa97b419408f00fbb2bcd8cda884646137ef6ab8f0bc0efd61516dde5882f9 (sha256 35aa97b419408f00fbb2bcd8cda884646137ef6ab8f0bc0efd61516dde5882f9), spec_fingerprint fd86eb9ab09aa054555305e9405e0ca0d623d01f76b8fb3f7e4bc2a4741557ec. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: fd86eb9ab09aa054555305e9405e0ca0d623d01f76b8fb3f7e4bc2a4741557ec; artifact_sha256: 35aa97b419408f00fbb2bcd8cda884646137ef6ab8f0bc0efd61516dde5882f9; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/dickinsonia_costata_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=2eab73577d2f595b..., datasets/dickinsonia_costata_turing_wavelength_s0/dickinsonia_costata_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=654790d69ff50dc8..., datasets/dickinsonia_costata_turing_wavelength_s0/dickinsonia_costata_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=9cde902e8577ea73..., datasets/dickinsonia_costata_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=5eef4d2dd1042991..., datasets/dickinsonia_costata_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=7d02cb51fc7fd66f...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-dickinsonia-costata-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and critical wavenumber k_c. | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v. | Bobrovskiy et al. 2018 cholesterol biomarkers and the White Sea 558 Ma horizon. | Evans et al. 2017 ovoid outline maintained by terminal module addition; Evans et al. 2021 posterior addition.; reconstructed_in_script: Cellular-tier Du, Dv distinct from the 2.2 mm organ-tier sibling. Septal count floor(2200/56) = 39. | Spectral Schnakenberg integration, diffusivity sweep, equal-diffusion ablation, and the length-unit anchor at 5.564e-5 m. | Gradient-energy ellipse and minor-axis ridge autocorrelation on the vendored photograph.; transfer_boundary: 56 µm is the slot's cellular-tier assignment. It is not a spacing reported by Bobrovskiy or Evans. | The photograph's ridge fraction (~0.0185 of the fitted major axis) is the organ-scale module repeat, not the 56 µm pitch. | Evans' sample is largely South Australian; the age used here is the White Sea horizon.; does_not_claim: That the spot lattice is the glide-symmetric module pattern of the fossil. | That the terminal GIF frame is a forward pixel prediction. It is the specimen photograph, the empirical endpoint of the growth sequence. | A calibrated millimetre reading off the ruler in the photograph.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Resolved in Pass 2: 12-frame 720x540 GIF ends on the Verisimilus fossil; cyan ellipse on the comparison figure.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Resolved in Pass 2: diffusivity scales 0.55..4.2, Pearson r = 0.999999999886.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Resolved in Pass 2: Du = Dv control decays to roundoff; censored ratio 4215.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Resolved in Pass 2: RMSE 0.061 µm, KS 0.125, CV of k ratio 6e-6, specimen aspect 1.8, circularity 0.882, coherency 0.561, ridge fraction 0.0185.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.59e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

