<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-dickinsonia-costata-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Dickinsonia costata cellular Turing wavelength, 56 µm, White Sea 558 Ma (Pass 2) (Dickinsonia costata)",
        "Dickinsonia costata cellular Turing wavelength, 56 µm, White Sea 558 Ma (Pass 2) faithfully reproduces Dickinsonia costata morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-dickinsonia-costata-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-dickinsonia-costata-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-dickinsonia-costata-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-dickinsonia-costata-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Dickinsonia costata specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-dickinsonia-costata-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Dickinsonia costata" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A calibrated millimetre reading off the ruler in the photograph.",
        "does_not_claim: That the spot lattice is the glide-symmetric module pattern of the fossil.",
        "does_not_claim: That the terminal GIF frame is a forward pixel prediction. It is the specimen photograph, the empirical endpoint of the growth sequence.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Cellular-tier Du, Dv distinct from the 2.2 mm organ-tier sibling. Septal count floor(2200/56) = 39.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Gradient-energy ellipse and minor-axis ridge autocorrelation on the vendored photograph.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Spectral Schnakenberg integration, diffusivity sweep, equal-diffusion ablation, and the length-unit anchor at 5.564e-5 m.",
        "reported_in_source: Bobrovskiy et al. 2018 cholesterol biomarkers and the White Sea 558 Ma horizon.",
        "reported_in_source: Evans et al. 2017 ovoid outline maintained by terminal module addition; Evans et al. 2021 posterior addition.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and critical wavenumber k_c.",
        "transfer_boundary: 56 µm is the slot's cellular-tier assignment. It is not a spacing reported by Bobrovskiy or Evans.",
        "transfer_boundary: Evans' sample is largely South Australian; the age used here is the White Sea horizon.",
        "transfer_boundary: The photograph's ridge fraction (~0.0185 of the fitted major axis) is the organ-scale module repeat, not the 56 µm pitch." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Dickinsonia costata (Late Ediacaran (White Sea, 558 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Zoophyta & Vermes (Cnidaria/Platyhelminthes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Dickinsonia" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-dickinsonia-costata-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/dickinsonia_costata_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Dickinsonia costata; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and critical wavenumber k_c. | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v. | Bobrovskiy et al. 2018 cholesterol biomarkers and the White Sea 558 Ma horizon. | Evans et al. 2017 ovoid outline maintained by terminal module addition; Evans et al. 2021 posterior addition.; reconstructed_in_script: Cellular-tier Du, Dv distinct from the 2.2 mm organ-tier sibling. Septal count floor(2200/56) = 39. | Spectral Schnakenberg integration, diffusivity sweep, equal-diffusion ablation, and the length-unit anchor at 5.564e-5 m. | Gradient-energy ellipse and minor-axis ridge autocorrelation on the vendored photograph.; transfer_boundary: 56 µm is the slot's cellular-tier assignment. It is not a spacing reported by Bobrovskiy or Evans. | The photograph's ridge fraction (~0.0185 of the fitted major axis) is the organ-scale module repeat, not the 56 µm pitch. | Evans' sample is largely South Australian; the age used here is the White Sea horizon.; does_not_claim: That the spot lattice is the glide-symmetric module pattern of the fossil. | That the terminal GIF frame is a forward pixel prediction. It is the specimen photograph, the empirical endpoint of the growth sequence. | A calibrated millimetre reading off the ruler in the photograph.]; phenomenon_size: 44 µm (4.42e-05 m, log10=-4.355 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 44 µm to 9.9 cm): 44 µm:dickinsonia-costata-bioelectric-polarity, 138 µm:dickinsonia-costata-vertex-packing, 2.2 mm:dickinsonia-costata-turing-wavelength, 4.4 mm:dickinsonia-costata-clock-wavefront, 9.9 mm:dickinsonia-costata-morphogen-condensation, 1.2 cm:dickinsonia-costata-elastic-buckling, 1.4 cm:dickinsonia-costata-flux-canalization, 1.9 cm:dickinsonia-costata-branching-tree" ;
